          #SpineAndHornLocalization.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The localization at the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendroidal+spine"} dendroidal spine
              inclusions is equivalently the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} left Bousfield localization
              at the set of dendroidal inner horn inclusions.
          %p
            This is
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#CisinskiMoerdijk"} Cisinski-Moerdijk, prop. 5.5, def. 6.2
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p By the nature of left Bousfield localization, it is sufficient to show that one localizing set of morphisms is contained in the weak equivalences of the other.
            %p
              In one direction, it is clear that every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+anodyne+morphism"} inner anodyne morphism
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendroidal+sets"} dendroidal sets
              is a weak equivalence in the localization at the horn inclusions. By the discussion at
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spine"} spine
            %p
              Conversely, one checks that the weak equivalences generated by the spine inclusions contain all inner anodyne morphisms (
              %a{:href => "#CisinskiMoerdijk"}> Cisinski-Moerdijk, prop. 2.8
              )
          #Corollas.num_defn
