          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              Being a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} category of presheaves
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Omega^{op}, sSet]
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable category
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CofibrantlyGenerated"}
              this means that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi gReedy
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Omega^{op}, sSet]_{gReedy}
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial model category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} left Bousfield localization
              at sets of morphisms.
          #CofibrationsAreNormalMonomorphisms.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_6 Proposition
            %p
              The cofibrations in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi gReedy
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Omega^{op}, sSet]_{gReedy}
              are precisely the simplicial-degree-wise
              %em normal monomorphisms
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendroidal+sets"} dendroidal sets
              (see
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "nlab/show/dendroidal%20set#NormalMonomorphisms"} here
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#CisinskiMoerdijk"}> Cisinski-Moerdijk, cor. 4.3
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_9 Proof
            %p
              The generating inclusions in prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CofibrantlyGenerated"}
              are the boundary inclusions of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representables
              in the product site
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta \times \Omega
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+Reedy+category"} generalized Reedy category
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "nlab/show/generalized%20Reedy%20category#NormalMorphisms"} there
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta \times \Omega
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
              contains no non-trivial automorphisms, this are just the degreewise dendroidal normal monomorphisms.
          #SimplicialEnrichment.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_7 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+Reedy+model+structure"} generalized Reedy model structure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi gReedy
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Omega^{op}, sSet]_{gReedy}
              equipped with the
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enrichment
              from remark
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TensoringAndEnrichment"}
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+model+category"} enriched model category
              over the standard
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
              – a
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
          .proof
            %h6#proof_10 Proof
            %p
              It is sufficient to check the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout-product+axiom"} pushout-product axiom
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensoring"} tensoring
              operation. So for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a : S \to T
              a monomorphism of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
              a degreewise normal monomorphisms in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi sSet
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Omega^{op}, sSet]
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CofibrationsAreNormalMonomorphisms"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (S \cdot Y) \coprod_{(S \cdot X)} (T \cdot X) \to T \cdot Y
            %p
              is a simplicial-degreewise normal monomorphism, which is a weak equivalence if either of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              or
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is. Since this coproduct is computed objectwise, this morphism is over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [n] \in \Delta
              the pushout of simplicial sets
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mi n
                        %mo ⋅
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi n
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi n
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (S_n \cdot Y_n) \coprod_{(S_n \cdot X_n)} (T_n \cdot X_n) \to T_n \cdot Y_n
                    \\,,
            %p
              where now the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensoring"} tensoring
              is that of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendroidal+sets"} dendroidal sets
              over sets, which is given by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
              of dendroidal sets,
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi n
                      %mo ⋅
                      %msub
                        %mi Y
                        %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                        %mrow
                          %mi s
                          %mo ∈
                          %msub
                            %mi S
                            %mi n
                      %msub
                        %mi Y
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_n \cdot Y_n = \coprod_{s \in S_n} Y_n
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
            %p
              Moreover, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
              of this morphism contains the image of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mi n
                      %mo ⋅
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_n \cdot f_n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \in T_n
              is the image of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendrex"} dendrices
              not in this image are also summand-wise not in the image of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilizer+groups"} stabilizer groups
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is a normal monomorphism.
            %p
              Finally, to see that the above morphism out of the pushout is a weak equivalence if either of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              or
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is, use that in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi fReedy
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Omega^{op}, sSet]_{fReedy}
              the weak equivalences are tree-wise those of simplicial sets. The statement then follows by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi sSet
                      %mi Quillen
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Quillen}
              being a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
              with respect to its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian monoidal
              category structure.
          %p Some of these properties are inherited by the actual model structure for dendroidal complete Segal spaces
          .num_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              The model structures
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi Segal
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Omega^{op}, sSet]_{Segal}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi cSegal
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Omega^{op}, sSet]_{cSegal}
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  are
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+simplicial+model+categories"} combinatorial simplicial model categories
              %li
                %p have as cofibrations precisely the simplicial-degreewise normal monomorphisms.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_11 Proof
            %p
              Since cofibrations and simplicial enrichment are preserved by left Bousfield localization, this follows from the analogous statements for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi sSet
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi gReedy
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Omega^{op}, sSet]_{gReedy}
          %h3#fibrant_objects Fibrant objects
          #FillerPropertyOfFibrantObjects.num_remark
            %h6#remark_4 Remark
            %p
              An object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi gReedy
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in [\Omega^{op}, sSet]_{gReedy}
              is fibrant, precisely if for every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tree"} tree
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \in \Omega
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi T
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi T
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi T
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X^{(\partial \Omega[T] \hookrightarrow \Omega[T])}
                    \:
                    X(T) \to X^{\partial \Omega[T]}
            %p
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibration"} Kan fibration
          .proof
            %h6#proof_12 Proof
            %p
              By prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FibrationsInGenReedy"}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                      %mo =
                      %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y = *
          #CompleteSegalBySpineLiftingAndHornLifting.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_8 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi gReedy
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in [\Omega^{op}, sSet]_{gReedy}
              be fibrant. Then the following conditions are equivalent
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi dsSet
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in dsSet
                  is a dendroidal Segal space, hence fibrant in
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msup
                            %mi Ω
                            %mi op
                          %mo ,
                          %mi sSet
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mi Segal
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Omega^{op}, sSet]_{Segal}
              %li
                %p
                  for every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spine"} spine
                  inclusion
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Sp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo ↪
                          %mi Ω
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp[T] \hookrightarrow \Omega[T]
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %mi Ω
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi T
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo →
                        %msup
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %mi Sp
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi T
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^{\Omega[T]} \to X^{Sp[T]}
                  is an acyclic Kan fibration;
              %li
                %p
                  for every inner
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horn"} horn
                  inclusion
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi Λ
                            %mi e
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo ↪
                          %mi Ω
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda^e[T] \hookrightarrow \Omega[T]
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %mi Ω
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi T
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo →
                        %msup
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi Λ
                              %mi e
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi T
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^{\Omega[T]} \to X^{\Lambda^e[T]}
                  is an acyclic Kan fibration.
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#CisinskiMoerdijk"}> Cisinski-Moerdijk, cor. 5.6
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_13 Proof
            %p
              By prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SpineAndHornLocalization"}
              Segal objects are equivalently spine-local and horn-local. By prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CofibrationsAreNormalMonomorphisms"}
              both the spine and the horn inclusion are morphisms between cofibrant objects in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi sSet
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi gReedy
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Omega^{op}, sSet]_{gReedy}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} left Bousfield localization
              and using that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi gReedy
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Omega^{op}, sSet]_{gReedy}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
              by prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SimplicialEnrichment"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi gReedy
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in [\Omega^{op}, sSet]_{gReedy}
              is local with respect to the spine / horn inclusions precisely if powering these into this object, remark
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TensoringAndEnrichment"}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CofibrationsAreNormalMonomorphisms"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout-product+axiom"} pushout-product axiom
              in a
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S = \{A \to B\}
            be a set of generating acyclic cofibrations for the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dendroidal+sets"} model structure on dendroidal sets
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi dSet
                      %mi CM
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet_{CM}
          #CompletenessByRightLifting.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_9 Proposition
            %p
              An object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi cSegal
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in [\Omega^{op}, sSet]_{cSegal}
              is fibrant precisely if
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  it is fibrant in
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msup
                            %mi Ω
                            %mi op
                          %mo ,
                          %mi sSet
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mi Segal
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Omega^{op}, sSet]_{Segal}
              %li
                %p
                  it has the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting property
                  against the set
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo →
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo →
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo →
                            %mi B
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi S
                            %mo ,
                            %mi n
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi ℕ
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\{
                        (A \to B) \bar \cdot (\partial \Delta[n] \to \Delta[n])
                        \\}_{(A \to B) \in S, n \in \mathbb{N}}
                        \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#CisinskiMoerdijk"}> Cis-Moer, cor. 6.5
            )
          .proof
            %h6#proof_14 Proof
            %p
              By prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalizationAtWeakOperadicEquivalences"}
              and the basic nature of left Bousfield localization.
          %h3#weak_equivalences Weak equivalences
          #WEDetectedOnCorollas.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_10 Proposition
            %p
              A morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
              between dendroidal Segal spaces is a weak equivalence in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi sSet
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi Segal
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Omega^{op}, sSet]_{Segal}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi cSegal
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Omega^{op}, sSet]_{cSegal}
              precisely if its components on the trees
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_n
              for all
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Corollas"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalences"} weak homotopy equivalences
              of simplicial sets.
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#CisinskiMoerdijk"}> Cisinski-Moerdijk, prop. 5.7
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_15 Proof
            %p
              By general properties of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} left Bousfield localization
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+objects"} local objects
              is a weak equivalence precisely if it is so already in the unlocalized model structure
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi sSet
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi genReedy
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Omega^{op}, sSet]_{genReedy}
              %em every
              tree. But by prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CompleteSegalBySpineLiftingAndHornLifting"}
              these are already implied by weak equivalences over the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spines"} spines
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
              which happen to be
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+colimits"} homotopy colimits
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
              and of corollas, and hence it suffices to have weak equivalences over these components in order to have them over all components.
          #WeakEquivalencesAreFullyFaithfulEssentiallySurjective.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_11 Proposition
            %p
              A morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
              of dendroidal Segal spaces is a weak equivalence in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi Segal
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Omega^{op}, sSet]_{Segal}
              precisely if it is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  fully faithful, def.
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FullyFaithfulMorphism"}
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+surjective+functor"} essentially surjective
                  in that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi η
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo :
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi η
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi η
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(\eta) : X(\eta) \to Y(\eta)
                  is a weak equivalence of simplicial sets.
          %p
            (See also
            = succeed ".)" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#CisinskiMoerdijk"}> Cisinski-Moerdijk, cor. 5.10
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_16 Proof
            %p
              Being essentially surjective is equivalent to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi η
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(\eta)
              being an equivalence. By prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WEDetectedOnCorollas"}
              it only remains to check that in this situation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              being fully faithful is equivalent to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(C_n)
              being an equivalence, for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %p
              By remark
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomotopyPropertyOfHomSpaces"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(C_n) : X(C_n) \to Y(C_n)
              is a weak equivalence for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is fully faithful, since weak equivalence are preserved by
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
            %p
              For the converse, consider for each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              the inclusion of
              %em all
              input and output colors
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mi n
                        %mo ;
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi η
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\coprod_{(x_1, \cdots, x_n; x)}
                    *
                    \\to
                    X(\eta)^{n+1}
            %p
              and similarly for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi η
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X(\eta)^{n+1}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+epimorphism+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} effective epimorphism in an (∞,1)-category
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mi n
                        %mo ;
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi n
                    %mo ;
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\coprod_{(x_1, \cdots, x_n; x)}
                    X(x_1, \cdots, x_n; x)
                    \\to
                    X(C_n)
            %p
              is an effective epimorphism, and similarly for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is fully faithful, then by the definition of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+epimorphism+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} effective epimorphism in an (∞,1)-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(C_n)
              as the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+colimit"} homotopy colimit
              of a diagram of equivalences. Hence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(C_n)
              is itself a weak equivalence.
          %h3#relation_to_other_model_structures Relation to other model structures
          %p
            We discuss the relation to various other model structures for operads. For an overview see
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/table+-+models+for+%28infinity%2C1%29-operads"} table - models for (infinity,1)-operads
          %h4#to_complete_segal_spaces To complete Segal spaces
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi dSet
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi dsSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta \in \Omega \hookrightarrow dSet \hookrightarrow dsSet
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tree"} tree
            with a single edge and no non-trivial vertex.
          %p
            Then
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice category
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi dsSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dsSet
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
            is evidently equivalent to that of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bisimplicial+sets"} bisimplicial sets
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ssSet
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi dsSet
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi η
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi dsSet
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  ssSet \simeq dsSet_{/\eta}
                  \\hookrightarrow
                  dsSet
                  \\,.
          %p
            By restriction along this inclusion, the above model structure reproduces the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+complete+Segal+spaces"} model structure for complete Segal spaces
          %h4#RelationToDendroidalSets To dendroidal sets / quasi-operads
          %p
            The model structure for dendroidal complete Segal spaces is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalent
            to the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dendroidal+sets"} model structure on dendroidal sets
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-categories"} quasi-categories
          %p We discuss in fact two Quillen equivalences, with right adjoints going in both directions:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#QuasiOperadsToDendroidalCompleteSegal"} From quasi-operads to dendroidal complete Segal spaces
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mo −
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi J
                      %mo ⊣
                      %msub
                        %mi Sing
                        %mi J
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi dSet
                        %mi CM
                      %mover
                        %munder
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi Sing
                              %mi j
                        %mover
                          %mo ←
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mo −
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mi J
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi sSet
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi cSegal
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      ({|-|_J} \dashv Sing_J) :
                      dSet_{CM}
                      \\stackrel{\overset{{|-|_J}}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{{Sing_j}}{\to}}
                      [\Omega^{op}, sSet]_{cSegal}
                      \\,.
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#DendroidalSegalSpacesToQuasiOperads"} From dendroidal complete Segal spaces to quasi-operads
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi i
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi sSet
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi cSegal
                      %mover
                        %munder
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mo ←
                          %mi i
                      %mi dSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      (i  \dashv )
                      [\Omega^{op}, sSet]_{cSegal}
                      \\stackrel{\overset{i}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{}{\to}}
                      dSet
          %h5#QuasiOperadsToDendroidalCompleteSegal Quasi-operads to dendroidal complete Segal spaces
          %p
            Recall from
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+Segal+space"} complete Segal space
            the basic example
            %em
              %a{:href => "complete+Segal+space#OrdinaryCategoriesAsCompleteSegalSpaces"} Categories as complete Segal spaces
            which shows how an ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is regarded as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+Segal+space"} complete Segal space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sing
                    %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sing_J(C)
            by setting
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sing
                    %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi n
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Core
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Sing_J(C) : n \mapsto N(Core(C^{\Delta[n]}))
                  \\,.
          %p
            Recall also that this and its generalization to
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a{:href => "complete+Segal+space#QuasiCategoriesAsCompleteSegal"} Complete Segal spaces of quasi-categories
          #SegalNerve.num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi J
                    %mo :
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo →
                    %mi sSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Delta_J : \Delta \to sSet
            %p
              for the cosimplicial simplicial set that in degree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+construction"} free
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[n]
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Delta_J(n) := N ( \{0 \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} \cdots \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} n \} )
                    \\,.
            %p We use the same symbol for the further prolongation to a cosimplicial dendroidal set
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi J
                    %mo :
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo →
                    %mi sSet
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mo !
                    %mi dSet
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Delta_J : \Delta \to sSet \stackrel{i_!}{\hookrightarrow} dSet
                    \\,.
            %p Moreover, we use the same symbol also for
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi J
                    %mo :
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo →
                    %mi dSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Delta_J : \Delta \times \Omega \to dSet
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi J
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ,
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi BV
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Delta_J : ([n], T) \mapsto \Delta_J[n] \otimes_{BV} \Omega[T]
            %p
              (where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi BV
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes_{BV}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boardman-Vogt+tensor+product"} Boardman-Vogt tensor product
              on
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendroidal+sets"} dendroidal sets
            %p
              The induced
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve+and+realization"} nerve and realization
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
              we denote
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo −
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi J
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msub
                      %mi Sing
                      %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi dSet
                      %mrow
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Sing
                            %mi j
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mo −
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mrow
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    ({|-|_J} \dashv Sing_J) :
                    dSet_{}
                    \\stackrel{\overset{{|-|_J}}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{{Sing_j}}{\to}}
                    [\Omega^{op}, sSet]_{}
                    \\,.
            %p
              So for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi dSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in dSet
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sing
                      %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi dSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Sing_J(X) :  (T, [n]) \mapsto Hom_{dSet}(\Delta_J[n]\otimes \Omega[T], X)
                    \\,.
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#CisinskiMoerdijk"}> Cis-Moer, 6.10
            ).
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p For
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Cat
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mrow
                    %mi Operad
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi N
                          %mi d
                    %mi dSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C \in Cat \stackrel{}{\hookrightarrow} Operad \stackrel{N_d}{\hookrightarrow}
                    dSet
            %p
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sing
                      %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo !
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Core
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Sing_J(C)
                    \:
                    i_!(
                    n
                    \\mapsto
                    N(Core(C^{\Delta[n]}))
                    )
                    \\,.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_12 Proposition
            %p
              The nerve and realization adjunction, def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SegalNerve"}
              constitutes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
              to the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dendroidal+sets"} model structure on dendroidal sets
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo −
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi J
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msub
                      %mi Sing
                      %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi dSet
                      %mi CM
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Sing
                            %mi j
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mo −
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi cSegal
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    ({|-|_J} \dashv Sing_J) :
                    dSet_{CM}
                    \\stackrel{\overset{{|-|_J}}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{{Sing_j}}{\to}}
                    [\Omega^{op}, sSet]_{cSegal}
                    \\,.
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#CisinskiMoerdijk"}> Cis-Moer, prop. 6.11
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_17 Proof
            %p
              First we show that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo −
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert -\vert_J}
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+Quillen+functor"} left Quillen functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi dSet
                      %mi CM
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet_{CM}
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout-product+axiom"} pushout-product axiom
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi dSet
                      %mi CM
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi BV
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (dSet_{CM}, \otimes_{BV})
              that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo −
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert -\vert_J}
              sends the generating (acyclic) cofibrations of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi Reedy
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Omega^{op}, sSet]_{Reedy}
              from prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CofibrantlyGenerated"}
              to (acyclic) cofibrations in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi dSet
                        %mi CM
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet_{CM}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi cSegal
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Omega^{op}, sSet]_{cSegal}
              are the same as those of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi sSet
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi Reedy
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Omega^{op}, sSet]_{Reedy}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo −
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert -\vert_J}
              sends the morphisms that define the localization, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ModelStructures"}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi dSet
                        %mi CM
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet_{CM}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi dSet
                      %mo ↪
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi sSet
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet \hookrightarrow [\Omega^{op}, sSet]
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi dSet
                      %mi CM
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet_{CM}
              (since all inner
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anodyne+morphisms"} anodyne morphisms
              are – this gives that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda^e[T] \to \Omega[T]
              is a weak equivalence – and all equivalences in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+model+structure+on+operads"} canonical model structure on operads
              are – this gives that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi BV
                    %mi J
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega[T] \otimes_{BV} J \to \Omega[T]
              is).
            %p
              So far this shows that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo −
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert - \vert_J}
              is left Quillen. To see that it is a Quillen equivalence, use that its composition with the left Quillen functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi dSet
                      %mi CM
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi gReedy
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i : dSet_{CM} \to [\Omega^{op}, sSet]_{gReedy}
              discussed in the
              %a{:href => "#DendroidalSegalSpacesToQuasiOperads"} companion section
              is evidently a Quillen equivalence.
            %p (…)
          .num_prop
            %h6#observation Observation
            %p
              If we write (as
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dendroidal+sets#Enrichment"} here
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi dSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in dSet
              normal and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi dSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in dSet
              fibrant
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mi Core
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    k(A,X) := Core(i^* [A,X]_{\otimes})
            %p
              for the maximax Kan complex inside the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi dSet
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi BV
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (dSet, \otimes_{BV})
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              fibrant, we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sing
                      %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Sing_J(X) : (T, n) \mapsto k(\Omega[T], X)_n
                    \\,.
          %h5#DendroidalSegalSpacesToQuasiOperads Complete dendroidal Segal spaces to quasi-operads
          %p Write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo :
                  %mi dSet
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ↪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi sSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  i : dSet = [\Omega^{op}, Set] \hookrightarrow [\Omega^{op}, sSet]
          %p
            for the evident
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            inclusion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendroidal+sets"} dendroidal sets
            into dendroidal simplicial sets induced by regarding a set as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+object"} discrete object
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
          #dSetsInjectedIntoSegalIsQuillenEquivalence.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p The inclusion
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi dSet
                      %mi CM
                    %mo ↪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi cSegal
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    i : dSet_{CM} \hookrightarrow [\Omega^{op}, sSet]_{cSegal}
            %p
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dendroidal+sets"} model structure on dendroidal sets
              to the model structure for dendroidal complete Segal spaces, def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ModelStructures"}
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#CisinskiMoerdijk"}> Cisinski-Moerdijk, prop. 4.8, theorem 6.6
            ).
          %p The following proof proceeds by passing through another Bousfield localization of a global model structure on dendroidal simplicial sets.
          #LocallyConstantModelStructure.num_defn
            %h6#definition_7 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi dSet
                      %mi CM
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi Reedy
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, dSet_{CM}]_{Reedy}
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+model+structure"} Reedy model structure
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+objects"} simplicial objects
              in the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dendroidal+sets"} model structure on dendroidal sets
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi dSet
                      %mi CM
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi LocConst
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mi id
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi id
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi dSet
                      %mi CM
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi Reedy
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [\Delta^{op}, dSet_{CM}]_{LocConst}
                    \\stackrel{\overset{id}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{id}{\to}}
                    [\Delta^{op}, dSet_{CM}]_{Reedy}
            %p
              for its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} left Bousfield localization
              at the set
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo ,
                        %mi T
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Ω
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S =
                    \\{\Delta[n] \cdot \Omega[T] \to \Omega[T]\}_{n \in \Delta, T \in \Omega}
                    \\,.
            %p
              We call this the
              %strong locally constant model structure
              on simplicial dendroidal sets.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#CisinskiMoerdijk"}> Cis-Moer, def. 4.6
            )
          #QuillenEquivalencedSetToLocConst.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_13 Proposition
            %p The functors
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi const
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msub
                      %mi ev
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi dSet
                      %mi CM
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi LocConst
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi ev
                            %mn 0
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi const
                    %msub
                      %mi dSet
                      %mi CM
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (const \dashv ev_0)
                    \:
                    [\Delta^{op}, dSet_{CM}]_{LocConst}
                    \\stackrel{\overset{const}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{ev_0}{\to}}
                    dSet_{CM}
            %p
              constitute a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#CisinskiMoerdijk"}> Cis-Moer, prop. 4.8
            )
          .proof
            %h6#proof_18 Proof
            %p
              The set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\Omega[T]\}_{T \in \Omega}
              is a set of generators, in that a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi dSet
                      %mi CM
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet_{CM}
              is a weak equivalence precisely if under the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+hom+space"} derived hom space
              functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}Hom(\Omega[T], f)
              is a weak equivalence, for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocallyConstantModelStructure"}
              is of the general kind discussed at
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
              in the section
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "simplicial+model+category#SimpEquivMods"} Simplicial Quillen equivalent models
          #FibrantObjectsInTheLocallyConstantModelStructure.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_14 Proposition
            %p
              The fibrant objects in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi dSet
                      %mi CM
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi LocConst
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, dSet_{CM}]_{LocConst}
              are precisely
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the Reedy fibrant simplicial dendroidal sets
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %li
                %p
                  such that for every
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
                  the morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi n
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_n \to X_0
                  is a weak equivalence in the
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dendroidal+sets"} model structure on dendroidal sets
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#CisinskiMoerdijk"}> Cis-Moer, 4.7 ii)+iii)
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_19 Proof
            %p
              The proof is again a special case of the general discussion at
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/simplicial+model%20category#SimpEquivMods"} Simplicial Quillen equivalent models
            %p
              By standard facts of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} left Bousfield localization
              a simplicial dendroidal set is fibrant in the locally constant model structure, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocallyConstantModelStructure"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi CM
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi Reedy
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, [\Omega^{op}, Set]_{CM}]_{Reedy}
              and moreover the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+hom-space"} derived hom-space
              functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi op
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi dSet
                          %mi CM
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mi Reedy
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}Hom_{[\Delta^{op},dSet_{CM}]_{Reedy}}((\Delta[n]\cdot \Omega[T] \to \Omega[T]), X)
              is a weak equivalence for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            %p
              We compute this derived hom space now in a maybe slightly non-obvious way, in order to get the result in a form that we can compare to the derived hom in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi dSet
                        %mi CM
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet_{CM}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+functors"} model structure on functors
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Set
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi CM
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi proj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, [\Omega^{op}, Set]_{CM}]_{proj}
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/%28infinity,1%29-categorical+hom-space#Framings"} framing
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat X
              of that:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi const
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi CM
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi proj
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi Reedy
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (const X \stackrel{\simeq}{\to}\hat X )
                    \\in
                    [\Delta^{op}, [\Delta^{op}, [\Omega^{op}, Set]_{CM}]_{proj}]_{Reedy}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[n]\cdot \Omega[T]
              is cofibrant in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi CM
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, [\Omega^{op}, Set]_{CM}]_{proj}
              (because
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[n]
              is representable and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi dSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega[T] \in dSet
              is normal), also
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi const
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} const \Delta[n]\cdot \Omega[T]
              is cofibrant in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi dSet
                        %mi CM
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi proj
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi Reedy
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, [\Delta^{op}, dSet_{CM}]_{proj}]_{Reedy}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ↦
                      %msub
                        %mi Hom
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mi op
                          %mo ,
                          %mi dSet
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi const
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}Hom(\Delta[n] \cdot\Omega[T], X)
                    \\simeq
                    \\left(
                    [n] \mapsto Hom_{[\Delta^{op}, dSet]}(const(\Delta[n]\cdot \Omega[T]), \hat X)
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p
              We claim now that such a resolution
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat X
              is given by (using the notation for core simplicial enrichement of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dSet
              = succeed ")" do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/model%20structure%20on%20dendroidal%20sets#Enrichment"} here
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ↦
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
