            %p
              are weak equivalences. Since the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\Omega[T]\}_{T \in \Omega}
              form a set of generators, this is the case precisely if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_n \to X_0
              is already a weak equivalence in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
