                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\Delta[0] \to \Delta[n]) \bar \times (\partial \Omega[T] \to \Omega[T])
                    \\,.
            %p
              This in turn means that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_n \to X_0
              has the right lifting property against the tree boundary inclusions. Since these are the generating cofibrations in the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dendroidal+sets"} model structure on dendroidal sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_n \to X_0
